35,2,1,talk,Servas,,It seems we face a choice between the burden of external appraisals and the risk of relying on unverifiable internal dashboards.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My findings suggest our ""wins"" were largely based on selling boring, stable tools to incumbents, not the disruptive growth we claim.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The data is concerning. Our reserves are being depleted faster than planned, and our credit line is far more restrictive than I hoped.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh boy, we have a problem! We have plenty of experts on the bench, but the recruiters can't find the actual boots-on-the-ground staff!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The data confirms my suspicion. External dependencies—security reviews and hardware supply chains—are the primary causes of our deployment delays.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Minako, if our reserves are tight, we cannot afford a holding that adds significant complexity or cost to our reporting process.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"Exactly. We should avoid any candidate that relies on high-churn, low-margin labor. Stability is more valuable than a flashy narrative right now.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,I agree. We need a candidate that requires minimal follow-on capital and doesn't rely on unbilled invoices for its valuation.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mio,,"But if we pick a company that needs a ton of field workers, we're going to be stuck doing the hiring ourselves again!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,We must avoid any candidate that requires deep integration into highly regulated environments or relies on custom hardware. The delays are too risky.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"A simple truth: the most elegant solution is often the one that requires the least amount of ""fixing"" at the end of the month.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Asuka,,I am looking for a business model that demonstrates high customer stickiness even when prices increase. That is the only real moat.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We must be disciplined. If a candidate's growth model demands frequent capital injections, it is a liability to the fund's current health.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mio,,I just don't want to spend my whole week on LinkedIn! Let's pick someone who already has their team or needs people we can actually find!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,I will prioritize a software-only solution that can be deployed in a standard cloud environment without a six-month security audit.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
